	(text "NIBBLE CARD COUPON: the 2N7000 + 47k cell in copper, measured before any card is trusted"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "98ce621e-eb5d-48b9-95d5-969c0d8343b6")
	)
	(text "26 transistors, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).  Power from the bus header (the hub, or 5 V on pins 1-2 and ground on 3-4; no other bus line is used).\nDrive IN, N1, N2, N3 from the 4-pin header (each has a 1Meg pull-down, so open = 0).\nMeasure at the test loops: TP_RING period (gate delay = period / 10), TP_FO1 vs TP_FO10 rise time (fan-out 1 vs 10), TP_NAND / TP_NOR output low\nwith all three inputs high, TP_BUS with the hub-style 10k pull-up, supply current with everything low.  Fill the numbers into docs/gate-cell.md."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 35.56 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ecad21e0-aec0-472c-80bc-ee695d8a070d")
	)
